{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And on that day… the Fish Gate</b> — it was in Jerusalem." "<b>From</b> — the armory, the king's second-in-command's residence, which is within the city." "<b>And a great crash</b> — outside Jerusalem, for mountains surround it."], :book :zephaniah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {1 "Reading משנה למלך as 'the king's second-in-command'; possibly refers to a royal official's quarters rather than an armory; the word הארמון ('armory' or 'palace') and its relationship to משנה למלך is textually uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zephaniah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zfanya"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:47:16.609328517Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}